{%- comment -%}
  Layer-2 tool registry (app-owned; spec §8.2) — the EXPLICIT registration list
  for this instance's MCP tools. Returns an array of { name, path } entries. Each
  `path` points at a tool directory under app/views/partials/mcp/tools/<name>/
  containing `manifest` (the declaration) and `call` (the handler), co-located per
  spec §5.2. A tool exists to agents ONLY if it appears here — dropping a tool
  directory is not enough, registration is a deliberate, reviewed one-line edit
  (the tool-poisoning mitigation as a structural property, §4.2).

  The engine loads each entry's manifest, validates it against the meta-schema,
  and serves only the valid ones; the registered `name` must match the manifest's
  own name (identity guard).
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign tools = '[]' | parse_json

  assign e1 = '{}' | parse_json
  hash_assign e1['name'] = 'search_events'
  hash_assign e1['path'] = 'mcp/tools/search_events'
  assign tools = tools | array_add: e1

  assign e2 = '{}' | parse_json
  hash_assign e2['name'] = 'create_event'
  hash_assign e2['path'] = 'mcp/tools/create_event'
  assign tools = tools | array_add: e2

  assign e3 = '{}' | parse_json
  hash_assign e3['name'] = 'broadcast_event'
  hash_assign e3['path'] = 'mcp/tools/broadcast_event'
  assign tools = tools | array_add: e3


  return tools
%}
